# XSH getpgrp()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getpgrp.001
anchor     functions/getpgrp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getpgrp.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       A child that made itself a group leader with setpgid(0, 0) gets
           its own process ID from getpgrp(), and a second child that
           joined that group gets the same value; before the change the
           first child's getpgrp() is the test process's group.
test       t/001-group.c
